00:49:12,631 --> 00:49:18,631
The Castle is a 1997 Australian comedy film directed by Rob Sitch, and written by Rob Sitch, Santo Cilauro, Tom Gleisner and Jane
Kennedy of Working Dog Productions, all veteran writers and performers on ABC's The Late Show and The D-Generation.

12
00:53:41,052 --> 00:53:47,052
The film stars Michael Caton, Anne Tenney, Stephen Curry, Anthony Simcoe, Sophie Lee and Wayne Hope as the Kerrigan family, as well as Tiriel Mora, Robyn
Nevin, Eric Bana, Costas Kilias and long time collaborator Charles "Bud" Tingwell (who had worked with the team since 1993 on "The Late Show").

13
00:58:09,473 --> 00:58:15,473
The film's title is based upon the English saying, repeatedly
referred to in the film, "A man's Home is his Castle.".

14
01:02:37,894 --> 01:02:43,894
Its humour plays on the national self-image, most notably the concept of
working-class Australians and their place in modern Australia.

15
01:07:06,315 --> 01:07:12,315
Shot in 11 days on a budget of approximately A$750,000, The Castle gained widespread acclaim in
Australia, where it is considered one of the greatest Australian films ever made.

16
01:11:34,736 --> 01:11:40,736
It grossed A$10,326,428 at the box office in Australia.

17
